rue"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/400"><img src="/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:79.9%;top:27.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg" alt="An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-staff-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff commissions</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff commissions</b>. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Not earned yet</span><em>The rental is ahead, or not paid in full</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pending approval</span><em>Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>You approved it; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded the payment; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Reversed</span><em>Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">By person shows each staff member&#39;s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Prices to review</b> lists prices typed by hand; <b class="gd-ui">Sourcing claims</b> lists staff who say they sourced a website request; <b class="gd-ui">Payments made</b> lists each payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Owner requests</b> lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company&#39;s share or of the cars&#39; rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change and approve</b> (your terms, with a note) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner&#39;s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner&#39;s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced an owner: the owner&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Sourced by</b>. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month&#39;s rentals</td></tr><tr><td>An owner a salesperson brought in</td><td>The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars&#39;, a partner&#39;s or a shareholder&#39;s cars</td></tr><tr><td>Customer service, finance, fleet, field staff</td><td>10% (also the field referral fee)</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off</td></tr><tr><td>On the owner statement</td><td>An owner&#39;s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner&#39;s car: from CarmaCars&#39; commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month&#39;s Sales tier) goes on the owner&#39;s next statement as an adjustment line.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-field-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Field pay</b>. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Clocked in and out</span><em>Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pay run started</span><em>Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>The figures are frozen, the period&#39;s hours are locked, the statements are numbered</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tab <b class="gd-ui">Pay run</b> shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings &gt; Program, Field pay). <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After the period ends, press <b class="gd-ui">Start the pay run</b>: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). <b class="gd-ui">Refresh the figures</b> takes in a change made since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The period&#39;s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (<b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> repeats it). The statement&#39;s number opens its PDF; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> gives the run for your accountant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> lists everyone&#39;s shifts of the period. <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hourly rates</b> shows each person&#39;s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with <b class="gd-ui">Set the rate</b> (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Field pay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overtime</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Vacation pay</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement</td></tr><tr><td>Deductions</td><td>None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer&#39;s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions that net to nothing</td><td>A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company statements</h2><p class="gd-p">CarmaCars&#39; own monthly statement, in twelve sections.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Download <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b>, <b class="gd-ui">PDF by owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">PDF by vehicle</b>, or press <b class="gd-ui">Email me the PDFs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Finalize</b> freezes the month. <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> works until then.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/reports</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:28%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.4%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.1%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.9%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from the revenue statement</h3><p class="gd-p">On an owner&#39;s page, the <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b> button sets <b class="gd-ui">How fees are paid</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Take from revenue statement</b>. Taken from the statement, the owner&#39;s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;. Approved, the invoice reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task <b class="gd-ui">Invoice ... back to the bank debit</b>.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The flat-rate agreements</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b> instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner&#39;s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK</b> is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-how-it-s-paid-bank-debit-or-deducted-from-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How it&#39;s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit on the 15th</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> (taken from the owner&#39;s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On an invoice, <b class="gd-ui">How it&#39;s paid</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For the first and last month, choose <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> on the Terms tab (or at approval).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the Terms tab, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the agreed one-off fees</b> makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner&#39;s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'advertising-and-owner-recruitment', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Marketing writes the text of every ad from the car''s own record, keeps track of where each ad is posted, tells the sales assistants when an ad needs updating, shows which channels bring bookings, drafts the week''s Facebook Page and Instagram posts and keeps the consent log for owner recruitment. Nothing is posted by the server: you post by hand, and Facebook Marketplace from the owner''s own profile.

## Write an ad

**Marketing** > **Listings**.

1. Choose the car and the channel (Facebook Marketplace, Kijiji, Craigslist, Instagram, Facebook Page or Google Business Profile) and press **Write it**.
2. Copy each part with its button: the title, the price line, the description (or caption), the hashtags and the tracked link. Each shows its length against the channel''s limit (a Kijiji title takes 64 characters, Craigslist 70, an Instagram caption 2,200, a Google post 1,500).
3. Add the photos in the order shown: the first is the cover. Open a photo to save it.
4. Post the ad on the site, then press **Mark as posted** and paste its address and the date.

- The text comes from the car''s record only: the rates, kilometres, deposit, delivery fee, who may rent it and the car code. A fact the record does not have is left out. No review, rating or claim is added.
- The tracked link opens the car''s page with utm_source (the channel), utm_medium and utm_campaign (the car code), so the request counts under that channel.
- A warning shows when the car does not take requests, has no daily rate, or shows sample photos (take real photos first: an ad shows the car itself).
- Facebook Marketplace is posted from the owner''s own Facebook profile in their browser: Meta does not take vehicle listings from business Pages. Kijiji takes one ad per car, in one category and one region. An Instagram caption cannot hold a working link: put it in the bio or a story link sticker.

## When an ad needs updating

**Marketing** > **Posted ads**, or the task in **Today** > **Staff tasks**.

1. A change of 3% or more in a car''s daily, weekend, weekly or 30-day rate, any change of its deposit, kilometres, extra-km price or delivery fee, or the car leaving the site marks each of its live ads Needs updating and opens a task for the sales assistants (for example Update the Kijiji ad and the car). The task says what changed, the new price line and the ad''s address.
2. Press **New text**, copy the new text and update the ad on the site.
3. Press **Mark the ad updated**. The task closes. Closing the task in Staff tasks counts too.
4. Car off the site: take the ad down and press **Taken down**. If the car comes back at the same rates first, the task is cancelled by itself.

> Good to know: The 3% is under **Settings** > **Program**, Advertising and owner recruitment. The rates are checked again every 6 hours, so a rate dated ahead is caught on its day.

## Bookings by channel

**Marketing** > **Bookings by channel**.

- Every request of the dates chosen counts once: under the source staff set on the booking, else the renter''s visit (the campaign source of a tracked link, or the site they came from), else a referral code, else how it reached us (phone, email, WhatsApp).
- Choose the last visit before the request or the first visit. A booking is a request that was confirmed, paid or completed; revenue is its rental charge after discounts. The months add up to the Bookings list.
- The visit is kept with the request when it is sent, so the source outlives the 90 days of visit history. A visitor who refused analytics cookies has no source.
- On a booking, the line Came from shows the source. Press **Set** to give it by hand when the renter told you (a Kijiji reply, a walk-in, word of mouth).

## Facebook Page and Instagram drafts

**Marketing** > **Social drafts**.

1. The week''s drafts are written from the fleet every 6 hours, for this week and the next: Monday a new car (published in the last 14 days) or a featured one; Tuesday the owner program; Thursday the cars free this weekend; Friday the requirements (Instagram); Sunday a price highlight or a seasonal trip (Facebook Page). Press **Write drafts for this week** to write them now.
2. Read each draft. Press **Edit** to change the caption, the channels or the day, then **Approve**; or press **Skip**.
3. Copy the caption for each channel (on the Facebook Page the tracked link is in the text; for Instagram copy the link for the bio), post it with the photos shown, then press **Posted on Instagram** or **Posted on Facebook Page** and paste the post''s address.

- Wednesday''s walkaround video and Saturday''s handover story are filmed by field staff. No renter is shown without written consent.
- Press **Add a post of your own** at the bottom of the week for anything else.

## Meta publishing (off until set up)

**Settings** > **Meta publishing**. Until it is on, every post is copied and posted by hand.

1. Make the Instagram account a professional account and link it to the CarmaCars Facebook Page.
2. At developers.facebook.com, create a Business app owned by the CarmaCars business portfolio. Give it the permissions pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, instagram_basic and instagram_content_publish, and make a long-lived Page access token. Meta may ask for App Review before posts are public.
3. Press **Enter the details**: the Page id, the Instagram account id and the token. The token goes to the vault; the page shows only its last four characters.
4. Press **Switch on**. Approved drafts then go out on their day and their post links are recorded; a refusal shows on the draft. Press **Switch off** or **Remove the token** at any time.

## Owner recruitment

**Marketing** > **Owner recruitment**.

Owners and co-hosts are found in classified ads. The anti-spam law (CASL) does not cover a live phone call, but an email or a text needs consent, names the sender and offers an unsubscribe. The lawyer confirms the approach before outreach starts.

1. Press **Add a lead**: paste the ad''s address, choose who is selling (a private seller, a dealer or a rental business) and type the name, the phone and the car from the ad. Nothing is collected from the classified site.
2. Call them with the script on the lead''s page and press **Log the call**. A yes needs their words ("Yes, text me the details"): they become express consent in the log. A no means do not contact, ever.
3. When the lead''s page says email or text is allowed, choose a template, check the words and press **Send**. The email adds CarmaCars'' name, mailing address and the unsubscribe link; the text ends with "Reply STOP to opt out." Texts wait for 8 am during quiet hours.

- Press **Record consent** for consent given another way: express (with its proof), implied by their inquiry (6 months), implied by a business relationship (2 years), a business address published with no "no solicitation" note (never a private seller), or one message after a referral (naming the referrer).
- The consent log is never edited: a change is a new line. An unsubscribe or a STOP reply adds a withdrawal by itself, and nothing more goes on that channel.
- A message without consent is refused with the reason. **Settings** > **Program** has a switch that stops all recruitment messages.

> Watch out: Keep the proof of an oral yes: a recording, or a note written during the call with the time. Consent you cannot show does not count.


## Owner pipeline

Open **Marketing** > **Owner pipeline**. Every prospective owner is one card, in one of seven columns: New, Contacted, Call booked, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded and Lost. Leads come from the owner form on the website, an owner''s referral link, Owner recruitment (classified ads) and **Add an owner lead**.

1. Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 after a lead comes in: the owner program in plain words (the car goes on our fleet insurance policy, we rent it out in Toronto and pay the owner every month; fees apply) and the link to apply. They are marketing emails: they wait behind every other email under the daily limit, go in the sending hours and carry the unsubscribe link.
2. They go only with consent: a website inquiry counts for 6 months, a classified-ad lead needs consent in its log, and a referral typed by staff gets one message only.
3. They stop when the lead replies (a text or a call from their number, or press **They replied**), when the stage changes, when they unsubscribe, and after the last one. **Stop follow-ups** and **Restart follow-ups** are on each card.
4. **Move** changes the stage (with a note, and why when lost). Agreement sent, Signed and Car onboarded also follow the owner''s records: an owner agreement sent or signed, a car on the site.
5. Sales and Customer service see the same board in the staff portal.

### Owner referral links

An owner''s link for new owners is `carmacars.ca/r/<their code>?to=owner` (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner''s car. It shows under **Owner referral credits** as due; pay it with the owner''s payout and press **Mark paid**.

## Listing channels

Open **Marketing** > **Listing channels**: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).

1. Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press **Update** to change them, **Add a channel** for a new one.
2. None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel''s address: **JSON**, **CSV** or **XML** (the XML is in the shape of Google''s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.
3. Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner''s car (01 Motors or any other). **Keep out** takes a car out of every feed.
4. **New key** ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.
