  '<p class="gd-p">Marketing writes the text of every ad from the car&#39;s own record, keeps track of where each ad is posted, tells the sales assistants when an ad needs updating, shows which channels bring bookings, drafts the week&#39;s Facebook Page and Instagram posts and keeps the consent log for owner recruitment. Nothing is posted by the server: you post by hand, and Facebook Marketplace from the owner&#39;s own profile.</p><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-write-an-ad" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Write an ad</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the channel (Facebook Marketplace, Kijiji, Craigslist, Instagram, Facebook Page or Google Business Profile) and press <b class="gd-ui">Write it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy each part with its button: the title, the price line, the description (or caption), the hashtags and the tracked link. Each shows its length against the channel&#39;s limit (a Kijiji title takes 64 characters, Craigslist 70, an Instagram caption 2,200, a Google post 1,500).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add the photos in the order shown: the first is the cover. Open a photo to save it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post the ad on the site, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as posted</b> and paste its address and the date.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The text comes from the car&#39;s record only: the rates, kilometres, deposit, delivery fee, who may rent it and the car code. A fact the record does not have is left out. No review, rating or claim is added.</li><li>The tracked link opens the car&#39;s page with utm_source (the channel), utm_medium and utm_campaign (the car code), so the request counts under that channel.</li><li>A warning shows when the car does not take requests, has no daily rate, or shows sample photos (take real photos first: an ad shows the car itself).</li><li>Facebook Marketplace is posted from the owner&#39;s own Facebook profile in their browser: Meta does not take vehicle listings from business Pages. Kijiji takes one ad per car, in one category and one region. An Instagram caption cannot hold a working link: put it in the bio or a story link sticker.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-when-an-ad-needs-updating" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When an ad needs updating</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Posted ads</b>, or the task in <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff tasks</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A change of 3% or more in a car&#39;s daily, weekend, weekly or 30-day rate, any change of its deposit, kilometres, extra-km price or delivery fee, or the car leaving the site marks each of its live ads Needs updating and opens a task for the sales assistants (for example Update the Kijiji ad and the car). The task says what changed, the new price line and the ad&#39;s address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">New text</b>, copy the new text and update the ad on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark the ad updated</b>. The task closes. Closing the task in Staff tasks counts too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Car off the site: take the ad down and press <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b>. If the car comes back at the same rates first, the task is cancelled by itself.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The 3% is under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Advertising and owner recruitment. The rates are checked again every 6 hours, so a rate dated ahead is caught on its day.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-bookings-by-channel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings by channel</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings by channel</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every request of the dates chosen counts once: under the source staff set on the booking, else the renter&#39;s visit (the campaign source of a tracked link, or the site they came from), else a referral code, else how it reached us (phone, email, WhatsApp).</li><li>Choose the last visit before the request or the first visit. A booking is a request that was confirmed, paid or completed; revenue is its rental charge after discounts. The months add up to the Bookings list.</li><li>The visit is kept with the request when it is sent, so the source outlives the 90 days of visit history. A visitor who refused analytics cookies has no source.</li><li>On a booking, the line Came from shows the source. Press <b class="gd-ui">Set</b> to give it by hand when the renter told you (a Kijiji reply, a walk-in, word of mouth).</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-facebook-page-and-instagram-drafts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Facebook Page and Instagram drafts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Social drafts</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The week&#39;s drafts are written from the fleet every 6 hours, for this week and the next: Monday a new car (published in the last 14 days) or a featured one; Tuesday the owner program; Thursday the cars free this weekend; Friday the requirements (Instagram); Sunday a price high