age and press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>. Within your limit you can also use <b class="gd-ui">Approve (within my limit)</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Approve and send the pay link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:69.4%;top:24%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.8%;top:98%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the &quot;First reply in opening hours&quot; measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Opening a request takes it for you: the others see &quot;Being answered by&quot; your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows &quot;Opens to you at&quot; a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-an-enquiry-on-an-example-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An enquiry on an example car</h2><p class="gd-p">Some cars on the site are marked &quot;Example car&quot;: samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after <b class="gd-ui">Free:</b> (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-request-from-a-vehicle-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request from a vehicle page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message (&quot;About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE&quot;) and an Enquiry task in To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-buyer-lead-from-a-buy-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A buyer lead from a /buy page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with &quot;Find me this car&quot;, and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The lead is in <b class="gd-ui">Buyer leads</b> (customer service: <b class="gd-ui">Owners and enquiries</b>), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop&#39;s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-to-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer to a caller</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a new customer</b>: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An offer that is out is changed in place: <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, change it, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Save without telling the renter</b>. No need to withdraw it first.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-new-quote-for-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New quote for a caller</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b>. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the lead came in, then the caller&#39;s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Create the request</b>. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1220/1260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1220" height="1260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:15.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:41.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:72.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:63.9%;top:85.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-edit-a-booking-a-fee-or-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking, a fee or the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter&#39;s details are corrected from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Money tab, Fees, <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (<b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>, For: the rental and fees).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves everything of the other record here.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-renter-messages-and-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter messages and Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>: search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To open a renter&#39;s private details, press <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>. The reason is kept in the access log.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/messages</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:48.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them. Photos are optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. How the owner signs: by email, or on paper.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and send to an Admin</b>. The application waits in the Admin&#39;s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owner-forms-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner forms (Forms C and D)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded, with the witnesses and the status.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness&#39;s signature and name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/300"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="300"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.6%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-rental-agreement-signed-on-paper" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A rental agreement signed on paper</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking. Under Signed on paper, press <b class="gd-ui">Record paper signature</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the Rental agreement, or the booking change the renter signed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan of every signed page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record signature</b>. It counts as signed, and the renter is not asked to sign again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> the signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>: they sign on their own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-booking-s-rental-agreements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The booking&#39;s rental agreements</h2><p class="gd-p">The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter&#39;s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer&#39;s policy number) are listed: type them and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>. Check-out stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every signature: a code to the signer&#39;s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-renter-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check renter documents</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task &quot;identity documents or coverage proof to review&quot;, or open the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Review</b> shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the name and date of birth, class G2 or G and valid past the return, the selfie matches, the coverage is active to the return date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin &gt; To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which credit cards include rental car coverage?</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters ask this often. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Send the renter <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span>: each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car&#39;s model year and trim so they can check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card&#39;s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer&#39;s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings &gt; Card coverage.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Review requests</b> shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The renter should be asked now anyway? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b>. Should never be asked? Press <b class="gd-ui">Do not ask</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows &quot;possible match&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> if it is them, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> if not, or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b> with the booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking, the card Review requests has <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> (for example after a call that went well) and <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> when the renter says they already left one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. Work it in order:</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Log a call</b></td><td>Record each call to the renter and what they said.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b></td><td>The first late notice email.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T14 (final notice)</b></td><td>The final notice.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Request disable</b></td><td>Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open an incident</b></td><td>When the car is not coming back as planned.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'sales', 'chapter', 'fleet', 'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Owner leads.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works. Answer requests and follow offers out.
2. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Save and send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **My work** > **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image: the name and date of birth match the booking, class G2 or G, valid past the return, no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **My work** > **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **My work** > **My sales**. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owner leads

1. Owner leads: each enquiry with the name, contact, car and status.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call the owner.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.
4. Owner applications, last 90 days, shows who applied and how far onboarding has come.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-04-leads-desktop-3402e913.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 400; address: carmacars.ca/va/leads; pins: 1 6.5 26.5, 3 94.8 44.0, 4 15.4 63.0")


## Owner pipeline

Open **Owner pipeline** (Sales or Customer service). Every prospective owner is a card in its stage: New, Contacted, Call booked, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded or Lost.

1. Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 and stop when the lead replies or you move the card.
2. After you talk to them, press **Move** and choose the stage. Add a note; when lost, say why.
3. They answered by email? Press **They replied**.
4. **Add an owner lead** for someone who called or walked in, or who was referred (a referral gets one email only).
